{"clock":35,"ops":[{"kind":"link","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"5bc05e6736eef355f718e4502926ce7aa0f91588","forge_id":"5981348114","number":"50","url":"https://github.com/guilbep/git-board/issues/50"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"5bc05e6736eef355f718e4502926ce7aa0f91588","field":"title","value":"proof: sync refs/notes/ci, so a reviewer pulls the proofs"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"5bc05e6736eef355f718e4502926ce7aa0f91588","field":"body","value":"\u003c!-- git-bug:00f87970cce0287158c7d7c59e02cf39d90c100c5a22fc227115c3b6012e06e9 --\u003e\nADR 0001 keeps each check's result as a signed line in `refs/notes/ci/\u003cwriter\u003e`. M4 (#46) writes and verifies them, but nothing moves them: a proof never leaves the machine that ran it, so a reviewer who pulls the repository finds none. The ADR's goal, async first (\"a reviewer pulls the repo, checks the status and trusts the check\"), needs this.\n\nThe ADR's section 2 sets the rules:\n- a clone pushes only its own `refs/notes/ci/\u003cwriter\u003e`, which only fast-forwards;\n- it fetches the other writers' refs into `refs/notes/remotes/\u003cremote\u003e/ci/*`, never with a `+` into its own namespace;\n- a reader takes the union of every writer's ref;\n- pushes go with git-board's sync, not one per run.\n\n\n- git-board's sync pushes this clone's `refs/notes/ci/\u003cwriter\u003e` and fetches every other writer's into `refs/notes/remotes/\u003cremote\u003e/ci/*`.\n- A check proven in one clone reads as proven in a second clone once both have synced, and `git board verify` agrees there.\n- A push of the clone's own ref that doesn't fast-forward is reported, never forced.\n- The verdict reads the remote-tracking refs as well as the local ones.\n- docs/ says how a reviewer without git-board fetches the notes (one refspec) and verifies a check with git and ssh-keygen.\n- Tested with throwaway repositories, never live remotes."}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"5bc05e6736eef355f718e4502926ce7aa0f91588","field":"status","value":"open"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"5bc05e6736eef355f718e4502926ce7aa0f91588","field":"labels","value":"kind:feat\nprio:p0\nstatus:ready"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"5bc05e6736eef355f718e4502926ce7aa0f91588","field":"assignees","value":"161889"}}]}